Port MediaTek's ECCCI modem stack (ccci_util_lib, ccmni, ccci_auxadc,
ccci_md_all, ccci_ccif, ccci_dpmaif) from OPPO's kernel_device_modules-6.12
to Linux 7.4 and the MT6858.

Applies with -p1 to eccci/, ccci_util/ and ccmni/ of
oppo-source/android_kernel_modules_and_devicetree_oppo_mt6993 at
4d505a4292dab3176a45fec66dc85debc362e24c
(kernel/kernel_device_modules-6.12/drivers/misc/mediatek), without their
Bazel files, beside include/mt-plat/{mtk_ccci_common,sync_write}.h and
include/conn_md_exp.h (conn_md/include). Adds the Kbuild files, compat
headers and stubs for vendor-only services, the 7.4 API updates, a real
of_get_named_gpio, the CCISM share memory the MT6858 modem asserts
without, and the GRO flush ccmni needs on 7.4. The MT6661 PMIC voter code
is stubbed, so no raw PMIC writes are built.

